Approach:

Upon downloading the pcap file and running it on wireshark we see there are various logs in a very quick sucession upon
inspecting the logs i noticed that the strings for this log was hidden in the form of base64 upon decoding one such string
"cGljb0NURg==" in cyberchef i got the output for b64 as "picoCTF" so i started looking through the traffic for logs that had 
strings ending with "==". Upon finding all of those and putting them all together in cyberchef i found the output of these 
strings as:- "picoCTF_34sy_tbh_4r_e5e8c78dnt_th4t{1t_w4s}" which ofc was jumbbled so i had to give it various attempts to 
unscramble it and finally get the flag for this ctf. 

